.Sh HISTORY
The curve functions were added in OpenSSL 1.0.2. The equivalent group
functions were added in OpenSSL 1.1.1. The
.Fn SSL_get_negotiated_group
function was added in OpenSSL 3.0.0.
.Pp
Support for ignoring unknown groups in
.Fn SSL_CTX_set1_groups_list
and
.Fn SSL_set1_groups_list
was added in OpenSSL 3.3.
.Pp
Support for
.Sy ML-KEM
was added in OpenSSL 3.5.
.Pp
OpenSSL 3.5 also introduces support for three
.Em hybrid
ECDH PQ key exchange TLS groups:
.Sy X25519MLKEM768 ,
.Sy SecP256r1MLKEM768
and
.Sy SecP384r1MLKEM1024 .
They offer CPU performance comparable to the associated ECDH group,
though at the cost of significantly larger key exchange messages.
The third group,
.Sy SecP384r1MLKEM1024
is substantially more CPU-intensive, largely as a result of the high CPU
cost of ECDH for the underlying
.Sy P-384
group.
Also its key exchange messages at close to 1700 bytes are larger than
the roughly 1200 bytes for the first two groups.
.Pp
As of OpenSSL 3.5 key exchange group names are case-insensitive.
.Pp
.Sy SSL_CTX_get0_implemented_groups
was first implemented in OpenSSL 3.5.
.Pp
Earlier versions of this document described the list as a preference
order.
However, OpenSSL's behavior as a TLS 1.3 server is to consider
.Fa all
supported groups as comparable in security.
